# RSF03-02: the browser check, as the shield sees it.
title A visitor without a pass gets a small task; a real browser solves it in a moment and holds a pass for an hour
row  visitor:box "A visitor" "too fast, or a checked page" | page:warnbox "The check page" "a task, no clicking" | pass:okbox "A pass cookie" "an hour, signed"
row  bot:nobox "A program" "no JavaScript: no pass" | site:okbox "Your page" "the same request again"
arrow visitor -> page "no pass"
arrow page -> pass "solved" go
arrow page -> bot "not solved"
arrow pass -> site "go" go
note The task gets harder the faster a visitor asks; verified search engines are never checked.
